Here's `rotate_right`, built by exactly mirroring `rotate_left` (swap every `left`↔`right`):

```c
static void rotate_right(rbtree_t *t, struct rb_node *x)
{
    struct rb_node *y = x->left;
    x->left = y->right;

    if (y->right != NIL) {
        y->right->parent = x;
    }

    y->parent = x->parent;

    if (x->parent == NIL) {
        t->root = y;
    } else if (x == x->parent->right) {
        x->parent->right = y;
    } else {
        x->parent->left = y;
    }

    y->right = x;
    x->parent = y;
}
```

Walking the mirror mapping against your `rotate_left` (`src/rbtree.c:162-185`):
- `y = x->right` → `y = x->left`
- `x->right = y->left` → `x->left = y->right`
- guard on `y->left` → guard on `y->right`
- the parent-side patch: `rotate_left` checks `x == x->parent->left` first (the "x is a left child" case); mirrored, `rotate_right` checks `x == x->parent->right` first
- `y->left = x` → `y->right = x`

Same precondition as `rotate_left`: this assumes `x->left != NIL` (i.e. `y` is a real node) — if `x->left` is `NIL`, `y` is `NIL`, and `y->right` reads `NIL_NODE.right`, which is `NULL` (zero-initialized), not `NIL`, so the `y->right != NIL` guard would wrongly pass and dereference `NULL`. Same latent issue as `rotate_left`, worth a one-line precondition comment on both when we wire them in.

Want me to write this into the empty `rotate_right` stub now (`src/rbtree.c:187-189`), or do you want to adjust anything first?

